<!-- Quality Standards Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Quality Control</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Sportswear Quality Standards | What to Inspect Before Shipping</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      AQL inspection standards are the industry benchmark for quality control in sportswear manufacturing. SDF Clothing follows AQL 2.5 for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, ensuring that only garments meeting strict quality standards reach our clients. This systematic approach involves inspecting a statistically significant sample from each production lot to identify defects before shipment.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Inline inspection occurs throughout the production process, not just at the end. Our quality team monitors cutting accuracy, sewing consistency, and decoration application at multiple checkpoints. This proactive approach catches defects early when they can be corrected efficiently, reducing waste and ensuring consistent quality across the entire production run.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Final inspection evaluates finished garments for seam strength, color fastness, sizing accuracy, and overall appearance. We check that sublimation prints are vibrant and crack-free, embroidery is secure without loose threads, and all labels and tags are correctly positioned. Our <a href="/quality-inspection-service" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">quality inspection service</a> provides detailed inspection reports with photos before shipment approval.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Common defects in sportswear include skipped stitches, puckered seams, misaligned patterns, and color bleeding. Sport-specific defects include uneven hemlines on running shorts, loose elastic in waistbands, and peeling numbers on jerseys. Our inspection process specifically targets these common issues based on garment type and intended use.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Reading an inspection report requires understanding defect classification and acceptance criteria. Major defects render a garment unsellable and must be rejected, while minor defects may be acceptable within specified limits. Our reports clearly categorize findings, provide photographic evidence, and recommend corrective actions for any identified issues.
    </p>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Performance testing goes beyond visual inspection. We conduct wash tests to verify color fastness, stretch tests for elastic components, and abrasion tests for durability on high-wear areas. These tests ensure that sportswear will perform as expected during actual use, maintaining appearance and functionality through repeated wear and laundering.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

